WEBVTT

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:06.100
Natsu!

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:10.280
Look! These are field horsetails!

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:14.910
There's so many of them!

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:18.650
Natsu!

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.710
Natsu, you always get sleepy when it's hot.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:27.710
Here, have some barley tea.

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:33.500
Natsu, I'll read a book for you.

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:39.010
Mr. Bear and Ms. Squirrel in the forest...

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:46.230
...stuffed lots of food into a wrapping cloth, and...

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:50.240
Natsu!

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:53.570
Natsu! No!

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:56.990
Don't hibernate!

00:00:58.030 --> 00:00:59.500
Natsu!

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:02.750
Natsu!

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:07.740
Every year, you cried about it,

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:11.140
so I stopped hibernating.

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:14.620
Hmm... I don't remember that.

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:20.500
Natsu...

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:22.860
And this time, you were—

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:23.820
Natsu...

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:28.480
I still want to go to high school in the city.

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:05.030
Episode 2:
"A Hard Road"

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:09.000
I still want to go to high school in the city.

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:12.670
Haven't we already been over this?

00:03:12.990 --> 00:03:15.790
The city is too dangerous for you.

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:19.090
It's fine.

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:21.410
What is?

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:23.420
Don't worry about it. It's fine.

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:25.890
Like I said, what is fine?

00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:39.900
What's that?

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:45.210
I know you just learned how to copy things from CDs to MDs,

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:49.680
but nobody uses or sells MDs and MD players anymore.

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:57.800
It was sad how proud you were when you told me.

00:03:58.130 --> 00:03:59.790
Look, Machi.

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:02.800
Your inability to keep up with the world

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:05.300
can be dangerous in the city.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:06.670
Shut up!

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:12.940
Stop nagging, you lazy bear!

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:17.860
Stop it! We settled this with that quiz the other day!

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:19.320
That was a unfair!

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:20.690
It's invalid! Invalid!

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:20.690
Ow! Ow!

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:25.260
Besides, before asking me, don't you need other people's permission?

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:28.230
What did Yoshio say?

00:04:28.770 --> 00:04:30.740
I'll support your decision...

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:33.620
as long as Natsu says it's okay. I'll even drive you there!

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:34.670
What about Fuchi?

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:36.130
Fuchi = Machi's and Yoshio's grandma

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:36.210
Ask Natsu.

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:38.750
I can't allow it.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:40.650
Ow! Ow!

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:44.300
What a baby! A bear is making your life decisions!

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:45.680
<i>What</i> did you say?!

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:45.680
You dummy!

00:04:46.170 --> 00:04:47.140
Ouch!

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:51.240
Meanie! Stupid! Idiot!

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:50.520
Hey! Don't hit my nose!

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:52.640
Dummy! Dummy! Dummy!

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:52.640
Hey!

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:53.640
Dummy...

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:02.510
Please, Natsu...

00:05:03.250 --> 00:05:05.610
My shyness, naivety...

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:08.410
and laziness...

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:10.980
I'll...

00:05:11.590 --> 00:05:13.780
try my best to correct them all.

00:05:20.030 --> 00:05:21.670
Okay...

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:24.670
Natsu!

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:28.640
But I'd worry too much if you left right now.

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:32.050
There's a lot you have to learn, all right?

00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:33.130
Okay!

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:37.930
Things like etiquette, common sense, how to read a map,

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:41.840
checking train schedules, how to make phone calls,

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:43.360
how to turn on a TV, and so on...

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:44.190
Okay!

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:48.160
I love you, Natsu!

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:51.760
That tickles, Machi.

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:55.550
Okay.

00:05:55.870 --> 00:06:00.370
I will now assign you your very first task!

00:06:00.370 --> 00:06:01.090
Okay!

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:08.180
No trial is too great for me. Bring it on!

00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:45.550
Finished!

00:06:56.830 --> 00:06:58.390
Read it for me, Natsu.

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:01.900
Go buy a HEATTECH product at Uniqlo.

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:05.680
Your handwriting is terrible.

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:08.900
Cut me some slack. I'm a bear.

00:07:09.230 --> 00:07:11.610
I'll give you two days.

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:13.340
Two days?!

00:07:13.340 --> 00:07:15.050
Starting tomorrow, so Saturday and Sunday.

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:18.560
There's no time to waste!

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:20.520
I have to get ready!

00:07:23.640 --> 00:07:28.340
Should I start typing these and printing them out?

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:31.340
But then how do I practice my handwriting?

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:39.090
I have to pick an outfit to wear to Uniqlo!

00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:44.190
There's a Uniqlo off the highway in the neighboring town.

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:47.120
I've driven past it a lot, but never been inside.

00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:49.920
It would take me an hour to bike there.

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:52.090
No... forty minutes.

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:55.470
Even so, my curfew is five o'clock.

00:07:55.470 --> 00:07:57.160
I can't afford to dawdle.

00:07:57.740 --> 00:07:59.850
It gets dark in the valley at four.

00:07:59.850 --> 00:08:02.000
I need to leave early in the morning.

00:08:02.350 --> 00:08:04.880
Considering all that, I should pick clothes

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:07.650
that I can move in without sacrificing style.

00:08:10.770 --> 00:08:11.860
But I can't,

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:15.610
because I haven't bought clothes since starting middle school.

00:08:15.610 --> 00:08:19.090
I just wear my school uniform or PE clothes all the time.

00:08:19.090 --> 00:08:23.060
Even at home, all I wear are these.

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:24.970
And I never go out.

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:27.360
Stupid Natsu!

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:29.980
This is too hard for a first task!

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:32.960
What even is HEATTECH, anyway?

00:08:32.960 --> 00:08:35.550
He knows I have trouble with English!

00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:40.030
What is HEAT... TECH?

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:44.420
HEAT... TECH?

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:46.410
That's strange.

00:08:46.410 --> 00:08:49.090
Judging from those words...

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:51.090
it's a heater!

00:08:52.480 --> 00:08:55.000
I always thought Uniqlo was a clothing store.

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:57.800
Do they sell heaters, too?

00:08:58.750 --> 00:09:01.840
So they sell clothes and they sell heaters.

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:02.810
Which means...

00:09:03.470 --> 00:09:05.810
Uniqlo is a hardware store?

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:09.770
For a hardware store, I don't have to worry what I wear!

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:11.790
My school uniform is fine!

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:19.070
But I wonder if a HEATTECH will be

00:09:19.670 --> 00:09:23.570
small enough to fit in my bike basket.

00:09:24.270 --> 00:09:26.900
It might be too big to bring back.

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:29.840
Also, it's a machine that gives off heat.

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:37.640
What if, when I'm riding along with it in the basket, it...

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:41.720
Natsu, do HEATTECH items... explode?

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:43.890
Natsu, do HEATTECH items... explode?

00:09:44.940 --> 00:09:45.570
Huh?

00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:48.970
Sorry. I couldn't hear you.

00:09:48.970 --> 00:09:49.730
Say that again.

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:52.830
Oh! Never mind! It was nothing!

00:09:57.760 --> 00:09:59.080
Phew!

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:02.340
Looks like I said something off base again!

00:10:02.340 --> 00:10:03.470
That was close!

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:07.240
It's probably just an electric foot warmer or something.

00:10:07.240 --> 00:10:11.710
They should just say so instead of trying to sound cool with English.

00:10:11.950 --> 00:10:16.170
Well, this'll be easy! What a simple errand.

00:10:21.990 --> 00:10:23.680
Is she going to be okay?

00:10:27.740 --> 00:10:31.090
The cloud cover's perfect! It's a silky, white sky.

00:10:31.090 --> 00:10:33.520
A perfect day to go out.

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:36.130
Now I don't have to worry about heatstroke.

00:10:36.130 --> 00:10:37.360
That's true.

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:40.060
It can't be sunny every day.

00:10:41.060 --> 00:10:42.780
See you later!

00:11:01.190 --> 00:11:02.470
Hm?

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:06.610
Hey! Hey there! Machi!

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:10.490
Machi! You can't cross!

00:11:10.490 --> 00:11:13.250
The road is closed today!

00:11:13.250 --> 00:11:15.230
The bridge got washed away!

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:27.670
It was an old wooden bridge, so...

00:11:27.670 --> 00:11:30.120
It must've rotted through.

00:11:31.020 --> 00:11:33.460
At least it only affects you and us,

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:36.560
since we rent fields from Fuchi.

00:11:36.900 --> 00:11:39.570
Don't worry, Machi.

00:11:39.570 --> 00:11:43.470
We'll have a way for you to cross by tomorrow!

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:48.480
Only one day left.

00:12:03.220 --> 00:12:05.660
A freshly placed log; a bridge across the river.

00:12:06.650 --> 00:12:10.100
A girl; isolated from the world. Machi.

00:12:11.200 --> 00:12:13.710
Is this log the bridge to her dreams?

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:17.610
See ya!

00:12:19.590 --> 00:12:23.090
I'm not <i>that</i> cut off from the world.

00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:28.510
Huh?

00:12:29.250 --> 00:12:31.270
My bike is gone.

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:35.550
Aunt Etsuko!

00:12:35.550 --> 00:12:37.990
Hm? Oh, hi, Machi.

00:12:37.990 --> 00:12:40.820
I can't find my bike.

00:12:41.090 --> 00:12:44.190
You can't find your bike?

00:12:44.560 --> 00:12:47.000
Oh... I'm sorry.

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:50.580
I bet my husband
rode it to the field.

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:54.830
Since it's Sunday, he must've
thought you wouldn't need it.

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:57.080
You can take Yoshio's bike,

00:12:57.580 --> 00:12:59.960
though no one wants to ride it.

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:11.100
It's heavy.

00:13:14.890 --> 00:13:16.730
The chair is soft.

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:21.110
Hm?

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:24.030
Machi! Going out?

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:24.990
Yep.

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:44.590
Do I always go this fast?

00:13:44.590 --> 00:13:47.090
Maybe it's because this bike is heavy.

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:58.560
Oh, no! I'm too young to die!

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:13.120
Noooo!

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:42.440
Natsu...

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:45.940
Help me, Natsu!

00:14:57.830 --> 00:14:59.620
My back itches.

00:15:55.760 --> 00:15:57.010
I'm not giving up here!

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:07.440
Walk, Machi!

00:16:08.480 --> 00:16:10.530
Crossing the mountain directly...

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:12.570
might actually be a shortcut.

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:16.200
This is my test...

00:16:16.200 --> 00:16:17.870
to reach as far as I can...

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:19.080
my dream!

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:31.590
Oh, if it isn't Machi!

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:34.680
What're you doing all the way out here?

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:37.350
You've already finished picking aralia shoots, haven't you?

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:38.470
Me?

00:16:38.470 --> 00:16:41.180
As you can see, I'm fishing this mountain stream.

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:44.060
Matsu's wife said he went fishing despite being drunk,

00:16:44.060 --> 00:16:46.190
so she asked me to check on him.

00:16:46.190 --> 00:16:48.770
By the time I got here, he was completely wasted.

00:16:48.770 --> 00:16:49.900
That's dangerous, you know?

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:52.360
I told him to stop, but he wants to bring something home.

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:54.740
So here I am, fishing for him.

00:16:54.740 --> 00:16:57.820
But I'm not catching anything either.

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:01.160
What? Uniqlo?

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:02.620
Want a ride?

00:17:04.410 --> 00:17:06.000
Okay, Matsu!

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:08.130
Let's finish up! We're going!

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:12.130
What? Did you catch something?

00:17:12.130 --> 00:17:15.430
Look! I caught a miko! A beautiful miko!

00:17:15.430 --> 00:17:19.140
Whoa! What a blessing! What a blessing!

00:17:19.510 --> 00:17:23.520
But, you know, I'm here to catch some trout today.

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:26.270
Geez, Matsu. You're so drunk.

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:28.150
It's dangerous. Your wife is worried, too.

00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:29.520
No, she isn't!

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:31.480
Like hell she's worried!

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:35.030
That evil wife of mine is always...

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:44.830
Machi, want some?

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:47.460
My doburoku sake is pretty good, you know.

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:49.750
She's a minor, Matsu.

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:52.300
And the Liquor Tax Law bans making doburoku.

00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:55.090
Uniqlo?

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:58.890
Are you daft? It's not a hardware store!

00:17:58.890 --> 00:18:01.640
And HEATTECH isn't a heater, either.

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:04.520
You're funny, Machi!

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:12.270
All right! I'm gonna buy gladiator sandals!

00:18:12.270 --> 00:18:13.820
Just kidding!

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:17.570
Maybe I'll get a pair of jeans, too.

00:18:20.570 --> 00:18:24.950
That will be 990 yen for the one item.

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:24.330
I'm gonna record Machi's growth!

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:26.540
What do you mean by growth?

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:29.080
Out of 1,000 yen, your change is 10 yen.

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:29.080
Is she buying her first bra?

00:18:31.380 --> 00:18:33.090
Good for you, Machi!

00:18:33.090 --> 00:18:34.340
Was that your first time?

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:36.590
Matsu! That's sexual harassment!

00:18:35.590 --> 00:18:36.590
Well, this calls for celebration.

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:38.010
We should make red bean rice!

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:42.600
She's angry! Machi's angry!

00:18:43.680 --> 00:18:46.430
I'm sorry, miko! Please forgive me!

00:18:48.770 --> 00:18:51.610
Gah! My doburoku!

00:18:51.610 --> 00:18:53.110
It returns to the rice field.

00:18:54.230 --> 00:18:56.690
Me, too? Why?

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:14.960
Did you bring back a HEATTECH product?

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:17.050
Yeah.

00:19:18.050 --> 00:19:20.590
Then why are you so glum?

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:25.930
I feel...

00:19:27.310 --> 00:19:30.100
like I can't do anything by myself.

00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:32.020
That's true.

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:39.280
I broke Yoshio's bike, too.

00:19:39.280 --> 00:19:41.360
You rode that thing?

00:19:41.360 --> 00:19:44.410
I ended up having him drive me to the store.

00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:48.040
I expected you to do that right off the bat.

00:19:58.840 --> 00:19:59.420
What?

00:20:01.010 --> 00:20:01.680
Hm?

00:20:02.970 --> 00:20:07.470
Would it kill you to tell me that sooner?

00:20:07.850 --> 00:20:10.480
If you had, I wouldn't have gotten all scratched up!

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:11.980
Machi.

00:20:13.350 --> 00:20:15.360
Putting aside how you got there,

00:20:15.360 --> 00:20:18.650
what were you thinking, trying to cross the mountain?

00:20:18.650 --> 00:20:21.320
You know how dangerous the mountain can be, right?

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:25.870
Why didn't you come back when the bike broke?

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:30.000
How long would you have walked if you didn't run into Yoshio?

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:31.040
Who cares?

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:34.080
I got what you told me to, okay?

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:36.420
I passed! I passed, didn't I?

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:40.760
Fine, you pass.

00:20:44.260 --> 00:20:48.310
There we go. All's well that ends well!

00:20:49.390 --> 00:20:51.680
Does she appreciate what happened?

00:20:51.680 --> 00:20:52.600
And?

00:20:52.600 --> 00:20:55.020
I haven't seen what you bought yet.

00:20:55.310 --> 00:20:57.190
Show me.

00:21:03.700 --> 00:21:04.570
Hm?

00:21:10.660 --> 00:21:14.870
No! Don't wear HEATTECH under the miko garb!

00:21:28.680 --> 00:21:29.760
Huh?

00:21:30.600 --> 00:21:34.270
Mom! Where's my bike?

00:23:22.410 --> 00:23:23.400
Kumamiko-chan!

00:23:25.460 --> 00:23:27.090
I'm hungry.

00:23:29.010 --> 00:23:30.840
We have some mirin-flavored crackers.

00:23:32.640 --> 00:23:34.640
What about the vanilla ice cream?

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:35.890
Here it is.

00:23:41.440 --> 00:23:44.310
Machi likes eating vanilla ice cream

00:23:44.310 --> 00:23:47.110
and mirin-flavored crackers together.

00:23:50.400 --> 00:23:54.070
Kumamiko.
